30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>What is the speakers’ opinion of the bike-sharing schemes in each of the following cities?</p><p><em>Choose&nbsp;<strong>SIX</strong>&nbsp;answers from the box and write the correct letter,&nbsp;<strong>A-G</strong>, next to Questions.</em></p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong><strong>Opinion of bike-sharing scheme</strong></strong></p><p><strong>Cities</strong></p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"matching-dnd-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>Amsterdam</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">25</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>Dublin</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>London</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>Buenos Aires</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>New York</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>Sydney</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div></div><div class=\"options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--matching\"><div class=\"dnd-panel-instruction\">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</div><div class=\"dnd-cards-container\"><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"A\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">A.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">They agree it has been disappointing.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"B\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">B.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">They think it should be cheaper.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">They are surprised it has been so successful.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"D\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">D.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">They agree that more investment is required.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"E\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">E.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">They think the system has been well designed.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"F\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">F.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">They disagree about the reasons for its success.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"G\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">G.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">They think it has expanded too quickly.</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":6}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-16-academic-listening-4-audio-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-c16-t4-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/13316-cambridge-ielts-16-academic-listening-4-audio-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c16-t4-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write&nbsp;<strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong>&nbsp;for each answer.</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong><strong>THE EXTINCTION OF THE DODO BIRD</strong></strong></p><p>The dodo was a large flightless bird which used to inhabit the island of Mauritius.</p><p><strong>History</strong></p><ul><li>1507 – Portuguese ships transporting <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> stopped at the island to collect food and water.</li><li>1638 – The Dutch established a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> on the island.</li><li>They killed the dodo birds for their meat.</li><li>The last one was killed in 1681.</li></ul><p><strong>Description</strong></p><ul><li>The only record we have is written descriptions and pictures (possibly unreliable).</li><li>A Dutch painting suggests the dodo was very <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li><li>The only remaining soft tissue is a dried <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li><li>Recent studies of a dodo skeleton suggest the birds were capable of rapid <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li><li>It’s thought they were able to use their small wings to maintain <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li><li>Their <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;was of average size.</li><li>Their sense of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;enabled them to find food.</li></ul><p><strong>Reasons for extinction</strong></p><ul><li>Hunting was probably not the main cause.</li><li>Sailors brought dogs and monkeys.</li><li><span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;also escaped onto the island and ate the birds’ eggs.</li><li>The arrival of farming meant the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t4-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;was destroyed.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-16-academic-listening-4-audio-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c16-t4-l-q1","part_id":"en-c16-t4-l-p1","group_id":"en-c16-t4-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"28th","correct_answer_variants":["28th"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_13264_1","order_index":1,"p